      "writtenOn": "2026-09-28T16:38:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In LCOV format (`BRDA:\u003cline\u003e,\u003cblock\u003e,\u003cbranch\u003e,\u003ctaken\u003e`), the 4th field is the branch ID and the 5th field is the taken count. The original regex `^(BRDA):(\\d+),(\\d+),(\\d+),([-\\d]+)` captured `BRDA` as group 1, so group 4 was the branch ID and group 5 was the taken count; checking `match.group(4)` was a latent bug in the original implementation that checked the branch ID rather than whether the branch was taken. `taken` correctly inspects the taken field. Added an explicit unit test `test_filter_coverage_file_brda_taken_tracking`, documented this in the commit message, and cleaned up all offset magic numbers across the script.",
